# RESEED (hand-harvest, local on fix/retirement, forward-only): §16 CRUMB I0 — the runtime-prelude
# INJECTION SCAFFOLDING (`docs/design/plano-s16-runtime-prelude-injection.md` §1). The build
# front-end now injects the compiler-shipped Teko runtime SOURCE into every ordinary program's file
# set, so the Teko-over-mmap arena is compiled INTO each program's own teko.c. What this harvest
# carries:
#   - **the injection mechanism (build front-end — `src/build/project.tks`)**: four new functions
#     wired into `frontend_parse`, right after the `main.tks` injection:
#       * `rt_inject_namespaces` — the runtime namespaces injected into every ordinary program in
#         link order: `teko::runtime` (the arena provider `arena.tks`) and `teko::sys` (the
#         const-only ABI values the arena references). The intrinsics the arena also uses
#         (`syscallN`/`ptr_word`/`word_ptr`/`load_u64`/`store_u64`) need no source — codegen lowers
#         them — so they are absent.
#       * `rt_prelude_source_path` — resolves each namespace to its shipped source relative to
#         `rt_dir()`: `arena.tks` beside the C runtime, `sys.tks` in the `<parent>/sys` sibling dir
#         (the same shape `assert_dir` derives for the assert seed).
#       * `rt_already_present` — the DEDUP GUARD: skips a namespace the project's own discovered
#         file set already declares, so the compiler self-image (which discovers `teko::runtime` +
#         `teko::sys` under its own `src/` root) is SKIPPED and its emitted teko.c stays
#         byte-identical.
#       * `artifact_wants_runtime_prelude` — restricts injection to `Artifact::Binary`: a library
#         kind (`Static`/`Shared`/`Package`) is linked INTO a binary that injects the runtime
#         itself, so injecting it into the library too would double-define every arena symbol once
#         the consuming binary loads the library's `.tkl` (the dedup guard cannot see across the
#         dependency boundary). A library gets its arena from the final link.
#       * `inject_runtime_prelude` — prepends the shipped runtime source files onto the discovered
#         file set, skipping the deduped namespaces; they flow through parse -> prune -> check ->
#         codegen like any source, emitting into the one teko.c.
#   - **DORMANT (I0 is SCAFFOLDING)**: `cg_arena_sym` is UNFLIPPED, so an ordinary program COMPILES
#     the injected Teko arena (dead code) but still USES the C arena. Behavior is unchanged; only an
#     ordinary program's emitted C grows to carry the (unused) Teko arena. The compiler self-image
#     DEDUPS the injection, so its own emitted C changes ONLY by the five new build functions above.
#   - Touch points: `src/build/project.tks` (the injection); packaging staging of the runtime `.tks`
#     set (`scripts/package_release.sh`, `install.sh`); the RF1 injection fixture
#     `examples/regressions/user_prog_arena_alloc` (a leaf, not in the self-image).
#
# GATE: SELF-REPRODUCE — CLEAN FIXPOINT (tc1 == tc2 == tc3).
#   - The injection is dedup-neutral for the self-build (its own discover already yields
#     `teko::runtime` + `teko::sys`, so the injection is skipped), so the only self-image delta is
#     the five new build-front-end functions themselves. gen0 (cc of the prior seed) and gen1 emit
#     byte-identical whole-tree C.
#   - C-route chain: gen0 (cc, `-pthread`, from the prior bootstrap) built the tree -> gen1; gen1's
#     emitted C == gen0's emitted C; the C-route fixpoint gate returns PASSED (gen2 == gen3 byte for
#     byte, gen2.c == gen3.c, 22678872 bytes). `TEKO_MEM_PARANOID=1` full compiler build exits 0
#     (the memory keystone — the C arena's poison path stays clean). RF1 `user_prog_arena_alloc`
#     (an ordinary allocating program) builds with the injected arena DEFINED in its emitted C
#     (`teko_teko__runtime__region_alloc` present, absent under the prior seed) and exits 0 on the
#     still-dormant C arena. Self-reported peak 5665.3 MB (within the 6 GB cap).
